From: Elwin Huang <s09289728096@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Apr 2025 17:04:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7603: clean up beacon queue before empty CAB
 return

Commit c03d84c0d018 ("wifi: mt76: mt7603: improve stuck beacon
handling") moved beacon queue cleanup to the beginning of the pre-TBTT
tasklet. When the CAB queue is empty, the tasklet now returns immediately
after queueing a new beacon and does not run another cleanup pass.

On MT7628 this makes software scans take about four to five seconds. The AP
does not service clients for most of that interval, which can make clients
disconnect during a site survey.

Clean up completed beacon descriptors before taking the empty-CAB return.
This restores the cleanup timing needed by MT7603 channel changes without
reverting the stuck-beacon recovery added by c03d84c0d018.

The regression analysis and this fix were originally proposed in upstream
mt76 issue #973, where the cleanup restored the previous scan duration.

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/issues/973
Signed-off-by: Joe Guo <joe@gainstrong.cn>
---
 mt7603/beacon.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7603/beacon.c
+++ b/mt7603/beacon.c
@@ -146,8 +146,11 @@ void mt7603_pre_tbtt_tasklet(struct task
 	} while (nframes != skb_queue_len(&data.q) &&
 		 skb_queue_len(&data.q) < 8);
 
-	if (skb_queue_empty(&data.q))
+	if (skb_queue_empty(&data.q)) {
+		mt76_queue_tx_cleanup(dev,
+				      dev->mphy.q_tx[MT_TXQ_BEACON], false);
 		return;
+	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(data.tail); i++) {
 		if (!data.tail[i])
